                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The game is an absolute delight. It looks beautiful, the tone of its world is super charming and it's a really cosy little thing to play through, with a decent number of things to do and see.\n\nHowever, by far the greatest thing about the game is the building system, specifically the limitless potential it has for creation of abhorrent defilements of biology no man should have ever conceived. Genuinely it is such a blast to design freaks of nature in this game and for that alone it is a 11/10 experience.\n\nThe only real problem I have with the game is that there is nothing like a dedicated creative mode. Currently I'm really wishing there was something like a special 30th level you could unlock with postgame quests or similar challenges that would just be a massive clear building area with no obstacles and a way to spawn whatever fossils you want in it. Again, this game is practically perfect for what it is, even without a dedicated sandbox, but if it had something like that I'd be returning to it on a regular basis just to make whatever.\n\nAlthough, I imagine with a little bit of elbow grease level 27 could be turned into a decent little sandbox. Will need to try touching it up a little and see how it turns out.",
